<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.3">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2025-12-12T14:58:24+00:00</updated><id>https://glenaestebal.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>A simple, whitespace theme for academics. Based on [*folio](https://github.com/bogoli/-folio) design. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Agentic AI</title><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Agentic-AI/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Agentic AI"/><published>2025-12-08T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-12-08T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Agentic-AI</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Agentic-AI/"><![CDATA[<p>I’m learning Agentic AI on a free course in <a href="https://huggingface.co/learn/agents-course/unit0/introduction"> huggingface.co </a> that discusses AI agents in theory, design, and practice and how agents work and how to build our own Agents using the latest libraries and tools.</p> <p>The course is composed of learning Agent concepts in theory, learning to use established AI Agent libraries, and applying concepts learned in real-world problems.</p> <h4 id="contents">Contents</h4> <ul class="task-list"> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Introduction to Agents</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Frameworks for AI Agents <ul class="task-list"> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>The SmolAgents Framework</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>The LlamaIndex Framework</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>The LangGraph Framework</li> </ul> </li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Use Case for Agentic RAG</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Final Project - Create, Test, and Certify Your Agent</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Bonus Unit 1: Fine-Tuning an LLM for Function-Calling</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Bonus Unit 2: Agent Observability and Evaluation</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Bonus Unit 3: Agents in Games with Pokemon</li> </ul>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="agentic-ai"/><category term="AI"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[a course on using, understanding, and building AI agents]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Cybersecurity 101 - Introduction</title><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101-Introduction/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Cybersecurity 101 - Introduction"/><published>2025-10-30T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-30T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101-Introduction</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101-Introduction/"><![CDATA[<p>This is an example post with image galleries.</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/9-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/9-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/9-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/9.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/7-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/7-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/7-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/7.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <div class="caption"> A simple, elegant caption looks good between image rows, after each row, or doesn't have to be there at all. </div> <p>Images can be made zoomable. Simply add <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">data-zoomable</code> to <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">&lt;img&gt;</code> tags that you want to make zoomable.</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/8-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/8-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/8-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/8.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" data-zoomable="" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/10-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/10-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/10-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/10.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" data-zoomable="" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <p>The rest of the images in this post are all zoomable, arranged into different mini-galleries.</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/11-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/11-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/11-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/11.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/12-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/12-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/12-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/12.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/7-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/7-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/7-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/7.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="cybersecurity-101"/><category term="cybersecurity101"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[this is what included images could look like]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Cybersecurity 101</title><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Cybersecurity 101"/><published>2025-10-28T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-28T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Cybersecurity-101/"><![CDATA[<p>A beginner-friendly learning path in <a href="https://tryhackme.com/paths"> TryHackMe </a> providing a strong foundation in computer security. It introduces core concepts in networking, cryptography, and operating systems (Windows, Active Directory, and Linux), while exploring both offensive and defensive security tools. The program also offers insight into real-world applications and career paths in cybersecurity.</p> <h4 id="contents">Contents</h4> <ul class="task-list"> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Introduction <ul class="task-list"> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Offensive Security Intro</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Defensive Security Intro</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Search Skills</li> </ul> </li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Linux Fundamentals</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Windows and AD Fundamentals</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Command Line</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Networking</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Cryptography</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Exploitation Basics</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Web Hacking</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Offensive Security Tooling</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Defensive Security</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Security Solutions</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Defensive Security Tooling</li> <li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" disabled="disabled"/>Build your Cybersecurity Career</li> </ul>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="cybersecurity-101"/><category term="cybersecurity101"/><category term="review"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[beginner friendly path for a solid introduction to the different areas in Computer Security]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Blog Introduction</title><link href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Blog-Introduction/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Blog Introduction"/><published>2025-10-27T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-27T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Blog-Introduction</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/2025/Blog-Introduction/"><![CDATA[<h3 id="-welcome-to-my-cybersecurity-journey">👩🏻‍💻 Welcome to my Cybersecurity Journey</h3> <p><br/>This blog is where I document my path in cybersecurity — from studying core concepts and exploring new tools to reviewing lessons and preparing for certifications.</p> <p>It’s my way of tracking progress, sharing insights, and building a record of everything I learn as I grow in this field.</p> <p>Along the way, I’ll also share slices of life outside tech. I love reading, I’m learning how to bake, I’m exploring journaling, and I have a deep love for music. Expect book ratings, baking experiments, travel snapshots, food pics, and a little playlist inspiration sprinkled throughout the blog — a personal touch alongside the cybersecurity content.</p> <p>Currently, I’m reviewing Cybersecurity 101 with this <a href="https://tryhackme.com/paths"> TryHackMe </a> path. I’m also in a little bit of a side quest at the moment. I’m learning about Agentic AI from <a href="https://huggingface.co/learn/agents-course/unit0/introduction"> huggingface.co</a>!</p> <p>You can follow my thoughts and progress here on my <a href="https://glenaestebal.github.io/blog/category/posts/"> posts </a> on this blog! 🐳</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="posts"/><category term="general"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[tracking my journey, past, present, and future — from my first steps in cybersecurity to everyday life, hobbies, and personal growth.]]></summary></entry></feed>